    "id": "wtv3ozo3xgouyweezufg6oe8",
    "text": "Paragraph\n\nBut what happens if we dim the light so much that only one photon passes through the slits at a time? Surprisingly, even when photons are detected one by one, the same interference pattern gradually builds up on the screen. This suggests that each photon somehow behaves like a wave, interfering with itself, even though it is detected as a single particle.\n\n+"
  },
