    "id": "d85c6c53-e75b-4220-bf89-e2e96d57881e",
    "text": "Multiple choice\n\nEach photon carries 1.80 eV and the surface work function is 2.00 eV. At ordinary intensities in the single-photon model, what happens if the intensity is doubled at fixed frequency?\n\nElectrons are emitted because each photon gains energy.\n\nNo electrons are emitted; each photon is still below threshold.\n\nElectrons appear after enough energy accumulates over time.\n\nThe work function decreases to 1.00 eV.\n\nSUBMIT\n\n\nIncorrect\nTAKE AGAIN\n+"
