    "id": "rdf3909ocq9p0ssvdt7v02kt",
    "text": "Paragraph\n\nThe energy of each photon depends on its frequency, not its intensity. Increasing the frequency of light increases the energy of each photon, making it more likely to eject electrons from a metal. Increasing the intensity means more photons are present, but each photon still has the same energy. That’s why only high-frequency light can cause the photoelectric effect, regardless of how bright the light is.\n\n+"
  },
