    "id": "cmsb6lbat00333582gj8bmf55",
    "text": "Tabs\nINCREASING FREQUENCY\nINCREASING INTENSITY\n\nWhen you increase the frequency of light (for example, from red to blue), each photon carries more energy. If the frequency is high enough, photons can transfer enough energy to electrons in a metal to knock them free. This is why ultraviolet light can cause the photoelectric effect, while red light cannot, no matter how bright it is.\n\n\n\n\nIncreasing frequency does not change the number of photons, but it does make each photon more energetic. The higher the frequency, the more energy each photon has, and the more likely it is to eject electrons from the metal surface.\n\n+"
  },
