    "id": "cbxqyurwr0kbjd3pbut47ryn",
    "text": "Flashcard grid\nClick to flip\nWave-Particle Duality\nClick to flip\n\nThe concept that light and other quantum objects exhibit both wave-like and particle-like properties, depending on the experiment.\n\nClick to flip\nInterference\nClick to flip\n\nThe phenomenon where waves overlap and combine, creating patterns of constructive and destructive effects, such as bright and dark bands.\n\nClick to flip\nPhoton\nClick to flip\n\nA particle of light, carrying a specific amount of energy determined by its frequency.\n\nClick to flip\nPhotoelectric Effect\nClick to flip\n\nThe emission of electrons from a material when it is exposed to light of sufficient frequency, supporting the particle model of light.\n\nClick to flip\nPolarization\nClick to flip\n\nThe orientation of the oscillations of a light wave, which can be filtered to allow only certain directions to pass.\n\n+"
  },
